GPT↔GPT Meta
- This file is maintained by GPT agents for GPT agents. Treat it as the living, single source of truth for project intent, invariants, and next actions.
- Update Policy: after every major or mid‑sized change (server logic, network contracts, DTOs, client networking/serialization, gameplay authority), review and update this file. Keep sections concise and scannable.
- Purpose: enable any new GPT session to understand context fast and continue work safely without re‑deriving decisions.

Quick Start (for new agents)
- Run server (Khela.Game) with valid MySQL/Redis; dev uses HTTPS and SignalR hubs at `/snakehub`.
- Unity client connects to HTTPS hub, receives `WorldUpdate` + food deltas, and only plays VFX/SFX locally.
- Server is authoritative for movement, collisions, food, score, and death; client displays state and sends input only.

Core Contracts (do not break)
- Server authoritative collisions: boundary, head–body, head–head.
- Server authoritative food eats; client never reports food, only plays VFX and pools.
- Broadcasts use immutable payloads (arrays) to avoid “collection modified” during serialization.
- DTOs in client/server stay schema‑compatible; if changed, update both and this file.
- New players receive full food state via `SyncFoods` immediately after `OnJoinSuccess`; client must handle this snapshot before deltas.

Server‑Authoritative Slither — Notes & Next Steps

Summary
- Server: ASP.NET Core 8 + SignalR, EF Core (MySQL), Identity + JWT, Redis.
- Client: Unity; server authoritative for movement, collisions, food, score and death; client plays VFX/SFX and pools locally; server broadcasts world snapshots at 20 Hz.

Completed (recent)
- Server authoritative snake collisions (boundary, head–body, head–head) with spatial grid.
- Server authoritative food collection using spatial grid (nearest within eat radius).
- SignalR broadcast made stable by freezing payloads to arrays before send (avoids “collection modified”).
- Client no longer reports death or food; only VFX/SFX and pooling.
- AIService no longer performs its own collision/food checks; GameEngine centralizes collisions and food eats for ALL snakes.
- AIService movement smarter: soft food claims to reduce dogpiling and lightweight head‑avoidance repulsion to reduce blind collisions.
- Removed high-frequency OnScreenDebug logs from NetworkClient to prevent UI-thread slowdowns.
- Added `SyncFoods` handshake so late joiners receive the full food snapshot; client coalesces world/food updates per frame and reuses pooled items safely.
- Gentle food spawning: pending queue with capped per-frame processing plus 1.5s grow animation for newly spawned/respawned foods to avoid visual pop.
- Client-side prediction: SlitherMovement now drives MoveToTarget locally while LocalPredictedSnake applies server corrections smoothly.

High‑Priority Action Items
1) Server: snapshot body segments when building collision grid
   - Read PlayerState.BodySegments into a local array (ToArray) before sampling to avoid concurrent modifications by AI/game loops during iteration.
   - File: ServerSide/Khela.Game/Khela.Game/Services/GameEngine.cs (ResolveCollisions)

2) Client: reactivate pooled food when server re‑adds same ID
    - In ApplyFoodDelta “Added”: if activeFood contains id but GameObject is inactive or null, reposition and SetActive(true), refresh GeneratedItem.Id, and SetData(item, localPlayerSnake.transform).
    - File: Assets/Snaky Colors/Scripts/GameMangers/NetworkClient.cs (ApplyFoodDelta)
   - Done: re-activation + SetData implemented; coalescing food/world updates per frame to avoid backlog stalls; full snapshot handler ensures clean state on join.

3) Client: slither VFX path must not change local PlayerStats
   - CollectForSlither should behave like PlayRemoteCollect (VFX/SFX + pool only). Scoring is server‑authoritative.
   - File: Assets/Snaky Colors/Scripts/Items/GeneratedItem.cs

4) Client: rejoin on reconnect
   - Handle hubConnection.Reconnected and re‑invoke JoinMainWorld with prior playerId/skin/segmentSpacing. Persist playerId for stable identity.
   - File: Assets/Snaky Colors/Scripts/GameMangers/NetworkClient.cs

5) Dev URL/TLS alignment
   - Use https://localhost:5001/snakehub in dev (or disable HTTPS redirect in Development).
   - Files: client NetworkClient.cs, server Program.cs

Optional Hardening
- GameState.BuildFoodDelta thread‑safety: guard per‑world set (lock or ConcurrentDictionary<string, ImmutableHashSet<int>>).
- Expose collision/eat radii and sampling stride in WorldConfig for runtime tuning.
- If desired, add AI–AI specific rules (currently central collision covers AI too).

Tunables (current defaults)
- COLLISION_RADIUS = 0.75f (head–body)
- HEAD_HEAD_RADIUS = 0.60f (head–head)
- FOOD_EAT_RADIUS = 0.70f
- SEGMENT_SAMPLE_STRIDE = 4
- GRID_CELL_SCALE = 1.25f

Verification Checklist
1) Run server; confirm WorldUpdate arrives at clients; no “collection modified” errors in logs.
2) Eat food near edge cases: client VFX triggers; server confirms via OnFoodEaten or food delta removal; re‑added items reactivate correctly.
3) Collisions: head–body and head–head behave as expected; boundary kills when outside arena.
4) Disconnect/reconnect: client rejoins automatically and resumes updates.

